    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="Inscr.">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Episc">Episc</ref> Inscr.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Episc. Inscr." corresp="#wit-q">(De officio episcopi.)</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Episc. Inscr." corresp="#wit-x">VII. Item.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin" corresp="#wit-x">VII. ITEM</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">[Bischofs Recht und Pflicht]</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">[A bishop's right and duty]</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="399"><ref target="clause:WlEp_2-to-2-1">Wl ep 2</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">The Latin is the Quadripartitus; Liebermann's Old English is from X (Oxford, Bodleian, Junius 121, f. 13b, written at Worcester c. 1065). In OE the text survives only as a chapter in the middle of the so-called Polity (a compilation of c. 1027–60), but was perhaps originally separate, as the Quadripartitus had it. Liebermann dates it c. 1000–1050 and gives the German title in brackets as his own.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
